<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madeira</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madeira is an archipelago in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a> off the coast of north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Portuguese navigators settled it in the early fifteenth century, making it one of the first possessions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>. It became a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> production, a model later applied in other Atlantic colonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madeira.jpg" alt="Madeira" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Brian Boru Vector: Nuno Tavares · CC BY-SA 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Madeira.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
